{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/552667-official-blog-post-diving-into-the-continuum","id":552667,"title":"[official blog post] Diving into the Continuum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-13T00:27:38-07:00","id":552667,"title":"[official blog post] Diving into the Continuum","content":"Ian talks why the Continuum is a continuum: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/diving-into-the-continuum-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/diving-into-t...ity-continuum/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T04:26:20-07:00","id":554141,"title":"","content":"Thanks for pointing this out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:50:03-07:00","id":555223,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the decision to go larger or smaller will be if a given era will also have a new character type, or if it will mostly be a matter of how different that era is. WWII for instance is reasonably fresh enough no one should really be confused.<br /> <br /> I also of course wonder if we will see any new options eventually beyond psion, nova, or daredevil/inspired. I suspect that the answer is nothing concrete planned but options open for now, although the newer version of Aeon may feature some playable aliens - the Qin certainly, and possibly others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:59:05-07:00","id":555252,"title":"","content":"Possible Eras:<br /> <br /> Post Aeon Space Opera<br /> <br /> Alt Aeon Post Apocalypse<br /> <br /> Alt Aeon Cyperpunk<br /> <br /> (These are all present to an extent in Aeon as core, but such settings would see greater focus. Plus, I love me some cyberware and I always wanted to see a White Wolf game with it)<br /> <br /> The 1990s, mostly as a joke<br /> <br /> The 1970s, not nearly as much a joke as you might think.<br /> <br /> The Cold War era, in general.<br /> <br /> WW II<br /> <br /> Victorian Era<br /> <br /> Wild West Era<br /> <br /> Pirates/Age of Sail Era<br /> <br /> Renaissance Era<br /> <br /> Classical Antiquity (Someone mentioned an ancient world game being Antiquity, and I loved that idea.)<br /> <br /> Precivilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T21:16:20-07:00","id":555268,"title":"","content":"And then when you have a suitably diverse enough number of settings, you make a time-traveler game, because time travel is really a complicated enough subject to deserve it's own book/game entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T00:06:38-07:00","id":555367,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't get too tied down in details, full access space-time travel may have access to 100+ trillion years of possibilities. If we focussed too strongly on human history we would miss out on the epic scale time can represent. I would like to see a Transhuman Space kind of post-human setting and perhaps a follow up space-opera where we can't be sure which species arose from human stock wee are so far in the future. Like Aasimov's Foundation, but with aliens. If that even makes sense.<br /> A single book with a nice mandate could cover human history quite neatly and let the other books cover less well documented settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T06:13:26-07:00","id":555566,"title":"","content":"While I appreciate the worldbuilding needed to wrap Trinity together, and to expand it to multiple genres / periods beyond, I know in practice I'm only really interested in psions saving humanity from enemies within and without. I wonder how many gamers will actually make use of the full Continuum, to any extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6254-paulchapman","name":"PaulChapman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:43:44-07:00","id":555741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/552667-official-blog-post-diving-into-the-continuum?p=555566#post555566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I appreciate the worldbuilding needed to wrap Trinity together, and to expand it to multiple genres / periods beyond, I know in practice I'm only really interested in psions saving humanity from enemies within and without. I wonder how many gamers will actually make use of the full Continuum, to any extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I think quite a few have been wanting to do exactly that since Nova's appeared in Aberrant - and I can see the appeal for an audience that never played 1st edition to have plenty of settings to drop basically anything into. So I'd image there's quite a market for it actually.<br /> <br /> Like you though, I'm only really interested in the story of Psions and mundanes in the 2120's era, and maybe an advancement of the Continuum for Psions beyond that point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T09:54:32-07:00","id":555818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/552667-official-blog-post-diving-into-the-continuum?p=555367#post555367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't get too tied down in details, full access space-time travel may have access to 100+ trillion years of possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>100 trillion years of possibility reminds me of this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;<i>The fact is that the universe is going to stop expanding and it is going to collapse in on itself. We've got to do something before it's too late.</i>&quot;<br /> &quot;<i>How much time do we have left?</i>&quot;<br /> &quot;<i>60 trillion years, 70 at the most.</i>&quot;<br /> &quot;<i>Oh, no.</i>&quot;<br /> - <b>Jack</b> and <b>Patrick</b> (<a href=\"http://en.memory-alpha.wikia.com/wiki/Star_Trek:_Deep_Space_Nine\" target=\"_blank\">DS9</a>: &quot;<a href=\"http://en.memory-alpha.wikia.com/wiki/Chrysalis_%28episode%29\" target=\"_blank\">Chrysalis</a>&quot;) </div> </div> </div>Granted, we've found out since this episode aired (October 28, 1998) that the Universe's rate of expansion isn't slowing down...it's <i>speeding up</i>. In other words, we're not headed for the Big Crunch; we're headed for the Heat Death of the Universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;<i>Oh, no.</i>&quot;<br /> - <b>Patrick</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T05:08:08-07:00","id":556766,"title":"","content":"Time travel back to the Trias age and BLAAM!! LaZer Dinos!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:21:45-07:00","id":558396,"title":"","content":"I'm somewhat the opposite of some people here; I have no interest in Psions or the Aeon era, but I'm all over Novas - and anything Adventure! related.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T10:22:56-07:00","id":558397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/552667-official-blog-post-diving-into-the-continuum?p=555566#post555566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I appreciate the worldbuilding needed to wrap Trinity together, and to expand it to multiple genres / periods beyond, I know in practice I'm only really interested in psions saving humanity from enemies within and without. I wonder how many gamers will actually make use of the full Continuum, to any extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that my group is already chomping at the bit to do a whole setting where the effects of one part of the Continuum will resonate with the other ones. I have been working on how to time out to make it concurrent, though. But yeah, we will explore all of the Continuum at one point or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/552667-official-blog-post-diving-into-the-continuum?p=556766#post556766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time travel back to the Trias age and BLAAM!! LaZer Dinos!!!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did someone say Kung Fury?<br /> Wait...Kung Fury makes SENSE now. The rules seem to back up being able to do it. Hrmmmm....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":786,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","user":"thedonnie","date":". 06-17-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T11:10:05-07:00","id":558470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/552667-official-blog-post-diving-into-the-continuum?p=558397#post558397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that my group is already chomping at the bit to do a whole setting where the effects of one part of the Continuum will resonate with the other ones. I have been working on how to time out to make it concurrent, though. But yeah, we will explore all of the Continuum at one point or another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Did someone say Kung Fury?<br /> Wait...Kung Fury makes SENSE now. The rules seem to back up being able to do it. Hrmmmm....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Remember: the future of the King Fury timeline is Far Cry 3: Blood Dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T11:16:57-07:00","id":576630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaulChapman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/552667-official-blog-post-diving-into-the-continuum?p=555566#post555566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I appreciate the worldbuilding needed to wrap Trinity together, and to expand it to multiple genres / periods beyond, I know in practice I'm only really interested in psions saving humanity from enemies within and without. I wonder how many gamers will actually make use of the full Continuum, to any extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>*waves hand* Ooo, now I want to run a campaign where Max Mercer is basically the Doctor for the Trinity Continuum! (Except he <i>is</i> the TARDIS.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/552667-official-blog-post-diving-into-the-continuum?p=558470#post558470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember: the future of the King Fury timeline is Far Cry 3: Blood Dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but now that we're talking time travel, is this a case of the egg laying the chicken? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T16:46:18-07:00","id":583989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/552667-official-blog-post-diving-into-the-continuum?p=555741#post555741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I think quite a few have been wanting to do exactly that since Nova's appeared in Aberrant - and I can see the appeal for an audience that never played 1st edition to have plenty of settings to drop basically anything into. So I'd image there's quite a market for it actually.<br /> <br /> Like you though, I'm only really interested in the story of Psions and mundanes in the 2120's era, and maybe an advancement of the Continuum for Psions beyond that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know my group would be interested, we've had mixed results meshing Daredevils and Psions in stories. I also have a soft spot for Novas.<br /> As for Mercer being the TARDIS I can live with this provided the pocket dimension is written where he is trapped and devoured...or Daleks are introduced because every game needs something screaming Exterminate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}